From 05bcc18ff02b56ae974b323a2dec41c927ae3b41 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maxwellslater <maxtslater@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 7 Jul 2026 12:25:32 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] feat(inventory): add first-stock affordance for zero-stock
 items (FND-13)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

A newly-created item has no inventory_stock rows, so listItemStock returns nothing:
the Stock-by-Hub table showed 'No stock rows yet. Use the edit controls' but there
were no per-row editors and Move Stock was disabled — the item could never receive
its first stock. Add an admin-only 'Add Stock' button + AddStockDialog that seeds
stock at a hub (also usable to top up / add a new hub).

Uses a new ADDITIVE route branch ({hubId, addQty} -> restoreToHub) rather than the
absolute set: per the 3-agent review, an absolute set on a stale hub list could
clobber a concurrent seed (lost update), whereas additive accumulates. Guards:
admin-only via MutationButton (hidden for read-only operators — the only reachable
forbidden path the review flagged), qty >= 1, and the button disables when every hub
already has a row. Reserves/total stay consistent (restoreToHub floors, resyncItemTotal
recomputes the item total). Retire semantics were already real (handleRetire PATCHes
status=RETIRED) — no change needed there.

Antagonist review drove: MutationButton gating (already correct), the set->additive
switch (its own recommended fix), qty>=1, and disable-when-no-hubs. tsc clean; the
inventory flows have no unit test for this path, so CI + a staging click-through are
the confirmation.
